560 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 384 0 R
/E (Electronic systems are an essential part of modern life, and almost every electronic device requires a stable, smooth and regulated DC power source for its proper functioning. Whether it is a small LED indicator, a microcontroller, a communication device, an amplifier, or a sensor, all require a specific DC voltage that must remain constant irrespective of fluctuations in the input power.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
561 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 384 0 R
/E ( The purpose of a regulated power supply is to ensure that the output remains stable, noise-free, and safe for all types of electronic components.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
562 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 384 0 R
/E (A regulated power supply converts high-voltage AC \(Alternating Current\) from the mains into low- voltage DC \(Direct Current\). This process involves several stages such as stepping down the voltage, rectification, filtering, and regulation. Each stage plays a crucial role in ensuring that the output is reliable and suitable for use in electronic circuits.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
563 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 384 0 R
/E (This chapter provides an in-depth explanation of each building block of a transformer-based regulated power supply with dual output \(9V & 12V\). It explains the working principles, importance, and purpose of each component in detail.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
