/P 384 0 R
/E (In our households, we commonly receive 230V AC power from the main grid. However, almost all modern electronic devices operate on constant DC voltages such as 5V, 9V, 12V, or 15V. These DC voltages remain fixed and do not change their polarity or magnitude with time. On the other hand, AC voltage continuously changes its polarity and magnitude \(50 times per second in India\). If such fluctuating voltage is applied directly to electronic components, they will immediately burn or malfunction.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
