818 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 390 0 R
/E (Inthis regulated power supplyproject, a 1.5V LED is used as a visual indicator to show the proper operation of each voltage regulator output. An LED \(Light Emitting Diode\) is a semiconductor device that emits visible light when an electric current flows through it. It operates on the principle of electroluminescence, where energy is released in the form of light as electrons recombine with holes inside the diode material.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
819 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 390 0 R
/E (The LED used in this project has a forward voltage of approximately 1.5 volts, which means it requires 1.5V across it to begin glowing. LEDs are known for their low power consumption, long life, and reliability, making them ideal for use as status indicators in power supply circuits. They typically operate at a very small forward current, usually between 10 mA to 20 mA, which ensures bright illumination without generating excess heat.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
