1068 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 397 0 R
/E (The transformer is the first and most critical component in the power supply circuit. Its primary function is to step down the high-voltage AC mains \(typically 230V AC\) to a lower voltage suitable for electronic circuits. In this project, a 12-0-12V, 1A center-tapped transformer is used. The center tap allows the creation of dual voltage outputs and simplifies the rectification process.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1069 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 397 0 R
/E (The transformer not only reduces voltage but also provides electrical isolation between the mains and the low-voltage section, which is crucial for safety. It operates on the principle of electromagnetic induction, where alternating current in the primary coil induces a voltage in the secondary coil. The transformer is designed to handle a maximum current of 1A, ensuring that the circuit can supply sufficient current to the load without overheating.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
